# Little Browser: tabs stay in their strip (docs/ux.md). A dragged tab outside every tab strip stays
# in its strip instead of detaching into a new window, and dragging all of a window's tabs (its
# only tab) moves them within the strip, as any tab drag, instead of moving the window. Over the
# page a tab can still be dropped to make a split view, except as a window's only tab, which has
# nothing to be split with.
